{"name":"creator-matrix-colour-repaired","manifest":{"title":"Colour Picker","description":"An offline colour picker with a selectable colour and a text label showing the current selection.","operations":[{"name":"ask","description":"Open the colour picker and choose a colour."}],"settings":[],"slots":[],"icon":null,"toolbar":null,"entry":{"kind":"surface","name":"notes"}},"spec":"# Domain rules

- The app must run entirely offline. It must not use the network, runtime AI, or styles.
- The colour select must have exactly these options: `red` with label `Red`, `green` with label `Green`, and `blue` with label `Blue`.
- A selection change must never write to or reset the select that caused the change.
- Opening the app must be read-only and must never run domain work.
- Repeating startup composition must be safe and must not duplicate controls, reactions, or notes.

# Ask

## When

When the person opens the app or invokes `ask`.

## Then

Compose the surface entry named `notes` cheaply and idempotently. The surface contains one colour select with the options `red` / `Red`, `green` / `Green`, and `blue` / `Blue`, plus one text note showing the selected label.

If the select is uninitialized, initialize it to the `red` option. If it already has a selection, preserve that selection and do not reset it.

Read the current surface revision and set the surface using that current revision. Do not perform any other domain work while opening.

## Afterwards

The person sees the colour select and the text note through the `notes` surface entry. The select has its existing selection, or `red` when it was previously uninitialized, and the note shows the corresponding label.

# Selection change

## When

When the person chooses a different option in the colour select.

## Then

Use the selection already stored by the select and update only the text note to the selected option's label. Do not call `Set` or otherwise write to the select.

## Afterwards

The select remains on the option chosen by the person, the note shows exactly `Red`, `Green`, or `Blue` for the selected option, and the reaction terminates without triggering itself again.","files":{"ask.cs":"using DigitalBrain.Apps;
using DigitalBrain.Apps.Signals;
using DigitalBrain.Flutter;
using DigitalBrain.Flutter.Select;
using DigitalBrain.Flutter.Text;
using DigitalBrain.Flutter.Surface;

await using var brain = await DigitalBrainClient.ConnectAsync(args);
var app = brain.Get<IApp>(brain.Setting("App")!);
var root = brain.Setting("App")!;
var surface = brain.Get<ISurface>(root + "/notes");
var select = brain.Get<ISelect>(root + "/colour");
var note = brain.Get<IText>(root + "/note");
var options = new[] { new SelectOption("red", "Red"), new SelectOption("green", "Green"), new SelectOption("blue", "Blue") };

await foreach (var request in brain.On<AppRequested>(app, brain.Stopping))
{
    await select.Set("Colour", options, "red");
    await note.Set("Red");
    var current = await surface.Read();
    await surface.Set(new SurfaceDefinition("Colour Picker", new[] {
        new UiChildRef(UIVocabulary.SelectType, root + "/colour"),
        new UiChildRef(UIVocabulary.TextType, root + "/note")
    }), current.Revision);
}"},"settings":{},"connections":{},"version":"0.2.0","status":2,"activity":["build started","Building Colour Picker","round 1: search_contracts, search_contracts, search_contracts, read_contracts","round 2: read_contracts","round 3: check_csharp","round 4: read_contracts","round 5: check_csharp","round 6: check_csharp","round 7: check_csharp","build finished"],"versions":[{"version":"0.1.0","savedAt":"2026-10-12T12:44:57.2235325+00:00"},{"version":"0.2.0","savedAt":"2026-10-12T12:45:42.9230421+00:00"}],"publishedVersion":null,"origin":null,"edited":true,"synapses":[]}
